    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0173" n="103" xml:id="pg103"/>

                <head>No. 51.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Logan to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 24,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Logan says that Iglesias has signed the treaty according to the bases already
                    announced. Chili will yield the north of Peru at once, and keep an army in the
                    center. Montero remains in possession of the south only. Peace will follow if
                    the United States Government recognizes Iglesias. If this is not done, however,
                    serious complications will ensue and peace will certainly be postponed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
